# nhl-api-ts reads NO environment variables.
#
# The NHL API is public and unauthenticated, so there are no keys or tokens to
# set. All configuration is passed in code or as CLI flags:
#
#   new NHLClient({ debug, timeout, followRedirects })
#   nhl-api-ts ... --debug --timeout <seconds> --no-follow-redirects
#
# Node.js settings that affect the SDK's HTTP requests (read by Node, not by
# the SDK). All are optional; uncomment to use.

# Route requests through a proxy. Requires NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 (Node >= 24).
# NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:8080
# NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1

# Trust an extra CA bundle (e.g. a corporate TLS-inspecting proxy).
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/ca.pem
